{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new utility functions and enhances existing ones to improve iterable handling. It adds support for strict ordering checks, lazy evaluation for specific selectors, and new windowing and grouping capabilities.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "The public API must expose `unique_in_window` as a function that yields unique items from an iterable within a specified window size. Additionally, `zip_broadcast` must be available to zip iterables of different lengths by broadcasting shorter ones."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "The library must provide `distinct_permutations` to yield distinct permutations of an iterable. It must also expose `one` to return the single item from an iterable or raise an error if not exactly one item exists, along with `strictly_n` to yield exactly n items."
    },
    {
      "id": "m04",
      "text": "The `is_sorted` function must accept a `strict` parameter to enforce strict ordering checks on the input iterable. The `sample` function must remain available for random sampling from iterables."
    },
    {
      "id": "m05",
      "text": "The API must include `before_and_after` to wrap an iterable with lookahead capability. It must also expose `convolve`, `nth_combination`, `remainder_iterator`, `sliding_window`, `triplewise`, and `true_iterator` as standard itertools recipes."
    },
    {
      "id": "m06",
      "text": "The function `is_scalar` must be exposed to check if a value is a scalar type. The functions `zip_broadcast` and `zip_equal` must be available for zipping iterables with broadcasting or equality length requirements."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "The library must provide `duplicates_everseen` to yield all items from an iterable while marking duplicates. It must also expose `duplicates_justseen` to yield only consecutive duplicate items, alongside `unique_in_window` and `zip_broadcast`."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "The `strictly_n` function must behave lazily, yielding exactly n items from the input iterable without consuming it entirely upfront."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "text": "The API must expose `duplicates_everseen` and `duplicates_justseen` for tracking duplicate items in iterables. The `minmax` function must be available to find both minimum and maximum values in a single pass."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all listed functions are correctly exported and documented in the main module interface."
}
